56. The method of claim 55, wherein the evolutionary distance is calculated by: aligning two sequences from the list of proteins; determining an evolution probability process by constructing a conditional probability matrix: p(aa aa'), where aa and aa' are any amino acids, said conditional probability matrix being constructed by converting an amino acid substitution matrix from a log odds matrix to said conditional probability matrix; 

 accounting for an observed alignment of the constructed conditional probability matrix by taking the product of the conditional probabilities for each aligned pair during the alignment of the two sequences, represented by 

 ; n and determining an evolutionary distance from powers equation p'=p (aa aa'), maximizing for P.
